<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The mark as the system splash screen shows it, on Android 12 and later.

  With nothing said, the splash shows the launcher icon — both layers of it, tile included, cut to a
  circle — so the app opened on a dark rounded disc of tile sitting on the page, which is the one
  place the tile is a box on a page with no other box on it. This is ic_mark, the artwork with its
  own disc and no tile, exactly as the welcome screen shows it; see that file for why the disc makes
  the tile unnecessary.

  SIZE. The splash draws its icon into a square and masks it to a circle two thirds as wide — the
  outer sixth on every side is cut away — and it scales the drawable to fill the square whatever the
  drawable's own size says. A layer-list item fixed at 160dp was tried first and came out filling the
  circle, notebook corners clipped, because the list's intrinsic size was 160dp and was scaled up to
  fit. So the inset is a fraction, which is relative to the bounds the system sets and cannot be
  scaled away: a fifth on each side leaves the mark at 60% of the square, inside the circle with a
  little room around the disc.
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:drawable="@drawable/ic_mark"
    android:inset="20%" />
